      "content": "It's understandable to feel concerned when experiencing these changes in your later pregnancy. Persistent swelling in your hands and face, along with seeing flickering lights or brief vision disturbances upon standing, could be signs of preeclampsia. Because these symptoms can be serious, it is very important that you contact your obstetrician or healthcare provider right away for a thorough evaluation. They can monitor your blood pressure and determine if further testing is necessary.",
